# Documentation Standards

<rule>
name: atlas_documentation
description: Standards for maintaining proper documentation across the codebase
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(?:md|mdx|js|jsx|ts|tsx)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)documentation|docs|readme|comment"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When creating or updating documentation:

      ## Code Comments
      - Use JSDoc for function and class documentation
      - Document complex algorithms and business logic
      - Keep comments up-to-date with code changes
      - Document edge cases and workarounds
      - Use proper annotations (@param, @returns, etc.)

      ## README Files
      - Include clear project description
      - Document installation steps
      - Provide usage examples
      - List dependencies and requirements
      - Include troubleshooting information

      ## API Documentation
      - Document all endpoints
      - Include request/response examples
      - Document error responses
      - Provide authentication information
      - Document rate limits and quotas

      ## Component Documentation
      - Document component props
      - Include usage examples
      - Document component variants
      - Provide accessibility information
      - Document state management

      ## Architecture Documentation
      - Document system architecture
      - Include data flow diagrams
      - Document integration points
      - Provide deployment information
      - Document security considerations

examples:
  - input: "Creating a new component"
    output: "Include JSDoc comments, document props, and provide usage examples"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>